# Contributing

Contributions should advance the project’s
[Purpose and Vision](README.md) while preserving its
[North Star](NORTHSTAR.md).

Before changing code, apply the relevant engineering guidance:

- [Engineering standards](docs/engineering/standards.md)
- [Testing](docs/engineering/testing.md)
- [Tooling and quality gates](docs/engineering/tooling.md)
- [DevSecOps](docs/engineering/devsecops.md)

Automated agents must also follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

## Releases and commits

- Follow [Semantic Versioning 2.0.0](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html) for
  releases and public contracts; mark breaking changes with a major version.
- Follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/)
  for commits; mark breaking changes with `!` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.
- The installed `commit-msg` hook rejects non-conforming commit messages.
- Release Please derives version bumps and `CHANGELOG.md` entries from merged
  commits, then opens the release pull request. Do not edit release versions by
  hand.

