## Required verification

Run every command documented in
[tooling.md](docs/engineering/tooling.md) before submitting or completing a
change.

Do not claim a check passed unless it was executed successfully.

## Dependencies

- Use the selected ecosystem package manager.
- Add and remove dependencies through native package-manager commands.
- Keep runtime, development and optional dependencies in their proper groups.
- Commit lockfile changes produced by the package manager.
- Never edit the lockfile manually.
- Remove dependencies made unused by the current change.
- Explain why each new dependency is needed.
- Apply the dependency and supply-chain requirements in
  [devsecops.md](docs/engineering/devsecops.md).

[[ profile_values.DEPENDENCY_COMMANDS_SECTION ]]

## Tests

- Follow the meaningful-evidence rules in
  [testing.md](docs/engineering/testing.md).
- Add tests for changed behavior and reproducible defects.
- Keep tests deterministic and isolated.
- Use only the test levels required by the affected behavior.
- Do not add tests solely to increase coverage.
- Do not call live external services.
- Use synthetic test data and safe placeholder credentials.

## Documentation

Update documentation in the same change when modifying:

- public behavior or APIs;
- configuration;
- architecture or dependency boundaries;
- setup or verification commands;
- project invariants;
- security requirements.

Do not add speculative documentation or implementation plans.

## Generated files

- Do not edit generated files directly.
- Change the owning source and regenerate.
- Review generated diffs before committing them.
- Run the project’s stale-generation check when one exists.

